### Page 1 of 3

```text
PUBLIC SERVICES COMMITTEE
MINUTES
A meeting of the Public Services Committee was held on Monday, June 16, 2025, in Council
Chambers and via electronic meeting, starting at 12:00 p.m. Those in attendance were as follows:
COMMITTEE MEMBERS:
Tom Segrave, Chairman; Dr. Michelle Aldrich; Dr. Kathy
Emmons; and Jeff White (via Zoom).
AGENDA ITEMS
9.
ORDINANCE _31 READING
— Amending portions of the Unified Development Code,
modifying provisions related to Park Impact Fees, including the timing of fee payment and
permitted uses of such fees, and making conforming amendments thereto.
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on 3l and final reading, seconded by Dr. Emmons.
Dr. Aldrich
moved to amend by substitute dated June 5, 2025, seconded by Dr. Emmons. Dr. Aldrich moved
to amend section 4.2.5(0(1) to strike August 30Lh and replace it with September 30th, seconded by
Dr. Emmons. Motion to amend the substitute carried by unanimous voice vote. Motion to amend
by substitute, as amended, carried by unanimous voice vote. Main motion, as amended, carried by
unanimous voice vote.
Seth Lloyd, Planning & Development Department Senior Planner, provided a staff report and
advised that a proposed substitute was provided following the previous committee meeting noting
the request for extending the date of reporting fees to annually on September 30th
10.
ORDINANCE —3 READING
— Amending portions of the Unified Development Code
regarding signage, to increase allowances for window signs and further clarifying
prohibited signs.
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on 31 and final reading, seconded by Dr. Emmons. Motion carried
by unanimous voice vote.
Seth Lloyd, Planning & Development Department Senior Planner, provided a staff report and
advised the proposed ordinance was amended at the previous meeting of the governing body. The
date of the most current document was clarified by staff.
11.
ORDINANCE —3 READING
— Annexing to the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, various
tracts of land completely surrounded by current city limits situate in northeast Cheyenne
generally located north of Dell Range Boulevard, east and west of Ridge Road and south
of Storey Boulevard.
Dr. Emmons moved to approve on 3”’ and final reading, seconded by Mr. White. Motion carried
with Dr. Emmons and Mr. White voting “YES” and Dr. Aldrich voting “NO.”
```

### Page 2 of 3

```text
Connor White, Planning & Development Department Senior Planner, provided a staff report and
advised there have been no changes since approval on 2 reading. Committee members Aldrich,
Emmons and White commented on the item.
12.
ORDINANCE —3”’ READING
— Amending the Official Zoning Map of the City of
Cheyenne establishing the zoning classifications of: AG
— Agriculture; MR
— Medium-
Density Residential; MUR
— Mixed-Use Residential; and, CB
— Community Business, for
land annexed to the City of Cheyenne generally located north of Dell Range Boulevard,
east and west of Ridge Road and south of Storey Boulevard.
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on 211(1 reading, seconded by Dr. Emmons. Motion carried by
unanimous voice vote.
Connor White, Planning & Development Department Senior Planner, provided a staff report and
advised there have been no changes since approval on 2 reading. Committee member Aldrich
commented on the item.
13.
ORDINANCE —2 READING
— Annexing to the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, a portion
of land generally located east of South Greeley Highway and north of Chalk Bluff Road.
(SPONSOR - MR. SEGRAVE)
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on 2h1 reading, seconded by Dr. Emmons.
Motion carried by
unanimous voice vote.
Brandon Gilchrist, Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report and Mark
Christensen, AVI P.C. was available for questions.
14.
ORDINANCE ---2” READING
— Amending the Official Zoning Map of the City of
Cheyenne to assign a Zoning Classification of A-2 Agricultural to a parcel of land annexed
to the City, generally located east of South Greeley Highway and north of Chalk Bluff
Road. (SPONSOR - MR. SEGRAVE)
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on 2° reading, seconded by Dr. Emmons.
Motion carried by
unanimous voice vote.
Brandon Gilchrist, Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report and noted the
proposed zoning is related to the previously proposed annexation.
15.
ORDINANCE 2m1 READING
— Amending Section 10.04.050, Obedience Required, of
the Municipal Code of the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, to clarify the default offense level
for violations of Title 10 of the Municipal Code. (SPONSOR
— MR. SEGRAVE)
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on 2°” reading, seconded by Dr. Emmons.
Motion carried by
unanimous voice vote.
```

### Page 3 of 3

```text
David Hopkinson, Deputy City Attorney, provided a staff report and committee member Emmons
commented on the item.
16.
ORDINANCE —2” READING
— Amending Section 6.08.180, Feeding Geese and Ducks
Prohibited, of Chapter 6.08, Animal Care and Control Regulations Generally, of Title 6,
Animals, of the Municipal Code of the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, to include seagulls
and extend the feeding prohibition to all property within city limits. (SPONSORS
— DR.
ALDRICFI AND MR. MOODY)
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on 2°” reading, seconded by Mr. White.
Motion carried by
unanimous voice vote.
David Hopkinson, Deputy City Attorney, provided a staff report and Eric Fountain, Compliance
Director, provided additional information. Committee members Aldrich and Emmons commented
on the item.
Public comments were made by Ward III Councilman Mark Moody and Zachary
Mangin.
There being no further items for the agenda to come before the Public Services Committee, the
meeting was adjourned at 12:29 p.m.
Submitted by,
Jennifer McClelland
Executive Assistant to the Cheyenne City Council
```
